            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="1310-1f13-9f81-588c" name="Cybork Body" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade" sortIndex="3">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="a582-ae90-d546-7bec" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="843a-f127-1785-8e18" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="4a4c-a773-bf77-c55f" name="Cybork Body" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork with a Cybork Body has a 5+ Invulnerable Saving Throw.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="1c6e-30dd-b07d-d6db" name="Invulnerable Saving Throw" hidden="false" targetId="97b3-810d-a09e-872b" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="9683-c025-4671-f49c" name="Bionic Bonce" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade" sortIndex="1">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="96af-9786-606c-17c1" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="e1d5-99b0-4452-dfd4" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="dd6f-15f8-bdca-16fe" name="Bionik Bonce" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork with a bionik bonce adds +1 to its armor saving throw.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="ecc3-4fa1-0c46-36ee" name="Bionik Arm" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade" sortIndex="2">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="0116-0e20-195e-5470" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="b3ef-acc0-26b2-9214" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="2387-3be4-2857-0335" name="Bionik Arm" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork with a Bionik Arm causes one automatic S4 hit in close combat at Initiative 6, but only if in base-to-base contact with the target. It also counts as an additional close combat weapon.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="0638-5dce-1f96-beec" name="Dok's Tools" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade" sortIndex="4">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="eb3f-7fae-79e8-26a7" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="887e-b20d-cbb4-8528" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="356b-99e6-7e57-4242" name="Dok's Tools" hidden="false">
              <description>Once per turn at the end of the enemy's shooting phase a Mad Dok with Dok's Tools may attempt to "heal" a wounded or killed model. Roll a D6. On a 1 the Ork suffers 1 wound and if reduced to zero wounds is removed as a casualty. On a 2-5 there is no effect. On a 6 the Ork regains 1 wound up to the maximum it started the game with.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="96" />
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="c174-d709-9cb9-c386" name="Boss Snikrot and Da Redskull Kommandos" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <constraints>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="true" id="3a8f-c40b-6120-7b0c" type="max" />
      </constraints>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="6ea4-d1a6-284a-9524" name="Ork Mob Rule!" hidden="false" targetId="1586-dbe5-3b2e-7590" type="rule" />
        <infoLink id="abd4-3f7a-23ea-077f" name="The Power of the WAAAGH!" hidden="false" targetId="7bb4-34ca-51f3-bb8c" type="rule" />
      </infoLinks>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="8829-0d9a-ed04-c645" name="Boss Snikrot" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model" sortIndex="1">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="4800-08a7-ba93-ec5c" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="9fe2-162e-5db2-32f4" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="597b-74ee-d8b3-b741" name="Unseen, Unheard" hidden="false">
              <description>The Redskull Kommandos are such experts at sneaking that any enemy unit which wants to fire at them must check to see if they can spot them first using the scenario special rules for Night Fighting. If Snikrot and his Kommandos are not within this distance in inches the enemy unit's firing is wasted - they blast away at half-seen shapes to no effect. If the battle is actually taking place at night, then the normal spotting distance is halved against Da Redskull Kommandos.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule id="ee30-c0c2-1e62-9456" name="Backstabbers" hidden="false">
              <description>Being expert Kommandos, Snikrot and the Boyz are especially good at eliminating sentries. Sentires have their initiative value when attempting to spot Snikrot and the Boyz and a sentry killed in close combat will only raise the alarm on a roll of 6 instead of 4+</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="dd7a-d19b-c82a-e181" name="Boss Snikrot" hidden="false" targetId="21a6-bf55-e0dc-f940" type="profile" />
