        <entryLink name="Feral Orks Armoury" id="c60a-66fe-c8ba-b834" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="2" targetId="a6f6-4091-0b1a-8e95" type="selectionEntryGroup" />
      </entryLinks>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Wyrdboy" id="3044-e034-0aad-1bf4" hidden="false" targetId="2196-8f4c-05a5-b2dc" type="profile" />
        <infoLink name="Independent Character" id="0a47-cb2b-e6e8-4cbc" hidden="false" targetId="4a60-7f7e-c37f-a4d6" type="rule" />
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Psychic Vomit" id="41fc-7a13-741f-e2ad" hidden="false" page="11" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
          <description>Unable to contain the Ork energies any longer the Wyrdboy vents to forth in a stream of green psychogenic energy. Place the flamer template with the narrow end touching the Wyrdboy. Each model even partially under the template suffers an automatic Strength 4 hit.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Gork'll Get 'Em" id="f348-9719-0672-e118" hidden="false" page="11" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
          <description>The Wyrdboy's belief in Mork and Gork is so complete that it causes a manifestation of their power. This takes the form of a large green fist or foot descending from above. This counts as a shooting attack. The Ork Wyrdboy must be able to see his target, and rolls to hit as normal.

Range 72"
Strength 8
AP -
Assault 1, Blast</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Minor Psychic Power" id="fd28-ca47-2f2a-b17e" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="10" />
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Minor Psychic Power" id="0e92-06c7-43f0-0ee8" hidden="false" targetId="69af-f095-551d-130c" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
