            <profile name="Ammo Runt" id="0902-e251-7662-91c5" hidden="false" typeId="1e16-2bd8-7cad-379b" typeName="Unit">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="WS" typeId="c704-6128-f143-935a">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="BS" typeId="7928-3a9b-6080-ed95">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="df03-6292-d3f5-f778">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="T" typeId="e5f6-94c4-de8c-5fa8">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="W" typeId="4dc2-c603-0bc5-0561">1</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="I" typeId="eeda-4fb4-901e-b70d">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="A" typeId="abbf-0d11-fd86-d938">1</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="f47e-b15a-8f58-703c">5</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="b309-5233-122f-82bb">-</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Ammo Runt" id="0efc-6eea-5e6f-84c8" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork model in base-to-base contact with an ammo runt may re-roll one To Hit dice during a shooting phase. The ammo runt is removed once the re-roll has been used.
The ammo runt may not be chosen as a casualtiy caused by enemy shooting, but Blast markers and template weapons will affect them as normal.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Attack Squig" id="1b3b-f1fc-ff7d-fa66" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="ecfe-2f5c-fa46-efa8" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Attack Squig" id="3132-9e61-a65f-3d2b" hidden="false" typeId="1e16-2bd8-7cad-379b" typeName="Unit">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="WS" typeId="c704-6128-f143-935a">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="BS" typeId="7928-3a9b-6080-ed95">0</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="df03-6292-d3f5-f778">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="T" typeId="e5f6-94c4-de8c-5fa8">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="W" typeId="4dc2-c603-0bc5-0561">1</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="I" typeId="eeda-4fb4-901e-b70d">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="A" typeId="abbf-0d11-fd86-d938">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="f47e-b15a-8f58-703c">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="b309-5233-122f-82bb">6+</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Iron Gob" id="3b6d-9da3-2fbd-b462" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="639e-3823-cfda-200b" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Iron Gob" id="14eb-eb51-712c-5c45" hidden="false">
              <description>A mob led by a Warboss or Nob with an Iron Gob add +1 to their Leadership value.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Bosspole" id="271e-858b-813e-fcf9" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="f069-b5c4-f5b9-7251" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="3" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Bosspole" id="efcf-77cc-7302-463b" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork mob trying to mob up with a mob carrying a bosspole may re-roll their Leadership test if they fail on the first try.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Boar" id="7aef-bb5c-bc63-5ace" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="5af2-96b5-c5d5-22b9" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Boar" id="53fd-5d32-d93a-def9" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
              <description>Rider counts as cavalry - see page 93 of the Warhammer 40,000 rulebook.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Cyboar" id="3ddf-fe9d-d30e-ba6c" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="ba1d-652f-766a-dd2d" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="15" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Cyboar" id="948c-e6e2-7557-c6da" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
              <description>The rider counts as cavalry - see page 93 of the Warhammer 40,000 rulebook. Cyboar is extremely tough, reinforced with steel plates and bionic limbs, has its tusks replaced by blades and has an injection device which pumps it full of stimulants. Because of the toughness of the Cyboar and its value as cover the rider counts as being in 'eavy armour and gets a +4 armour save. The bionic augmentation makes the Cyboar a potent additional weapon granting the rider an additional close combat attack. During assaults and sweeping advances, models mounted on a Cyboar that pass through difficult terrain are killed on 1-3, as the Cyboar has a tendency to butt rocks and trees.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="'Eavy Armor" id="e36e-254b-3116-ac6c" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="09cf-3215-249b-945b" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="8" />
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="'Eavy Armor" id="bd26-e69a-3110-aea0" hidden="false" targetId="e312-e1c4-31fb-733d" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Frag Stikkbombz" id="134e-e24d-02a5-75bd" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="0a9a-c915-b9ac-7952" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="1" />
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Frag Grenades" id="b821-4236-c998-cf50" hidden="false" targetId="cedc-c0a1-ffd3-1b51" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Shiny Bitz" id="60a6-45c6-71ea-f04d" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="2bab-55c1-6054-7061" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="3" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Shiny Bitz" id="9b92-5252-1669-83d8" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
              <description>Feral Oaks are superstitious in the extreme and will sometimes get the idea that an otherwise useless object is really powerful talisman. An Ork with shiny bitz may re-roll one failed Armour save once in a game.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Grot Styboy" id="7bed-a3c9-f116-f99e" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="2d98-efd6-7a91-2498" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="2" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Grot Styboy" id="624b-57b0-1643-8524" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
              <description>A Grot Styboy is adept at tending to Boars and Cyboars and can provide valuable assistance for a Pigdok. When a Pigdok attempts to dope a unit he may add 1 to his dice roll for each Styboy assisting him. </description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Krak Stikkbombz" id="bb60-8460-b73e-4dd9" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="2e2f-92df-d5da-8f90" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="2" />
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Krak Grenades" id="7a07-250f-df13-44dd" hidden="false" targetId="9c1b-bf93-059b-27f5" type="profile" />
          </infoLinks>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Flash Furs, Skull Trophies, Toof Necklace" id="a3c5-3d8c-e280-52c3" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="815e-d285-e65d-3976" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="2" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Flash Furs, Skull Trophies, Toof Necklace" id="4724-a794-969a-dd98" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
              <description>Huntas who have managed to stalk and kill a particularly powerful or dangerous prey will wear its pelt, or take its skull as a badge of honour. These count as two models when calculating mob size for Mob Size tests only.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Squighound" id="bed0-5030-96d3-329c" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="d7ee-e437-9e88-5d52" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Squighound" id="185f-284e-e34a-e2e7" hidden="false" typeId="1e16-2bd8-7cad-379b" typeName="Unit">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="WS" typeId="c704-6128-f143-935a">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="BS" typeId="7928-3a9b-6080-ed95">0</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="df03-6292-d3f5-f778">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="T" typeId="e5f6-94c4-de8c-5fa8">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="W" typeId="4dc2-c603-0bc5-0561">1</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="I" typeId="eeda-4fb4-901e-b70d">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="A" typeId="abbf-0d11-fd86-d938">1</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="f47e-b15a-8f58-703c">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Sv" typeId="b309-5233-122f-82bb">-</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Squighound" id="4208-ddf2-52ef-be20" hidden="false">
              <description>A Slaver with a Squighound in base-to-base contact may re-roll Leadership tests and Moral checks for the Grot Mob or Big Gunz battery he is leading.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Super Cyboar" id="ecf9-6937-be4c-3e04" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="e4b6-01e5-76cf-cbe4" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="30" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Waaagh! Banner" id="f426-29c4-06c1-ed87" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="9d59-b2cd-b92e-e7c3" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="false" type="max" value="1" />
            <constraint id="eb20-6895-8cc1-f634" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="20" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Waaagh! Banner" id="ca84-834c-310c-61ce" hidden="false">
              <description>Any mob that has one or more models within 12" of the banner may re-roll their Power of the WAAAGH! test when they charge.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Warpaint" id="7771-396e-67dc-2c75" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="74fb-b495-709f-d3a6" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="3" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Warpaint" id="491c-dc30-361a-8266" hidden="false">
              <description>Feral Orks often daub themselves in dyes and paints that the Wyrdboy has prepared in the hope that some of his latent psychic powers are absorbed in the mix. A model protected by warpaint is not affected by psychic powers on a D6 roll of 6+. The power still works, the any character that makes his save will be unaffected.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Wyrdboy Stikk" id="1c81-1779-62e4-51c1" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="0200-33fd-b28e-f4f3" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Wyrdboy Stikk" id="54a5-1375-45f4-f89f" hidden="false" page="12" publicationId="aca0-89fc-f496-a111">
              <description>Wyrdboyz frequently carry copper staves to give themselves some protection against 'Eadbangs. When a Wyrdboy with a Wyrdboy Stikk suffers an 'Eadbang he re-roll the Strength of the attack.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Feral Ork Junka Upgrades" id="f160-3060-32b3-cf86" collapsible="true" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Armor Plates" id="9d56-a9a6-ad42-7e9c" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="da45-dc13-0050-ddfd" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Armor Plates" id="4a01-0f67-3220-880e" hidden="false">
              <description>Roll a D6 for each glancing or penetrating hit caused against the vehicle. On a 6 the hit is ignored.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Big Grabber" id="bb27-db4b-252d-2bf5" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="6683-7d6f-ee10-42cc" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Big Grabber" id="ba1f-a76d-7d95-a1b3" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12".
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target's speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Boarding Plank" id="0f2d-8b52-5be5-e171" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="5c7a-d244-36ab-aef5" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Boarding Plank" id="bcaf-1416-99e9-2e72" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12".
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target's speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Bolt-on Big Shoota" id="87c9-6948-5e54-bf6a" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="d069-f50f-38b5-0dc2" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="10" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Bolt-on Big Shoota" id="799f-473b-381e-520f" hidden="false">
              <description>A bolt-on big shoota can only be mounted on a wartrukk. It can be fired by one of da boyz onboard who is a passanger as long as the wartrukk itself does not move more than 12" that turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Reinforced Ram" id="5fb6-47b0-bd40-8541" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="6787-e3f8-a7ca-a0ad" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Reinforced Ram" id="cb35-ec13-bff8-8667" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12".
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target's speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Stikkabomb Chucka" id="e256-bbe8-265a-0e82" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="8d56-5b65-3af3-d6d9" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="3" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Stikkabomb Chucka" id="9a2d-5dd3-a2dc-ac55" hidden="false">
              <description>A vehicle or Dreadnought equipped with stikkbomb chuckas can make a Tank Shock attack even though it isn't a tank. A vehicle may not move more than 12" and attempt to tank shock and a Dradnought can only attempt a Tank Shock attack in its movement phase. In the assault phase it must move into close combat instead. If a proper tank is equipped with stikkbomb chuckas any tank shock it inflicts has an extra -1 modifier to the troop's Morale check.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Wrecker Ball" id="11a3-c28b-0992-c0cb" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="aae0-8b1d-e463-df93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="5" />
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Wrecker Ball" id="5494-5690-d41f-a75a" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12".
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target's speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="dade-2d82-e565-0a18" name="Mixed Armor" hidden="false">
      <description>When the Ork player makes armor saves before removing casualties from a unit that has models with different armor saves he uses the best armor saves as long as the Orks wearing that type of armor are in the majority. Any casualties removed after saving throws have been take must come from amongsth the most heavily armored Orks first.
If heavier armored Orks are in the minority use the worse armor saves and take the casualties from the lightly armored Orks instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1586-dbe5-3b2e-7590" name="Ork Mob Rule!" hidden="false">
      <description>If an Ork mob fails a moral or pinning check, roll 2D6. On a roll equal to or less than the number of Orks (ignore Gretchin) left in the mob than the Orks instead pass the test. An Ork mob of twelve or more models will therefore always pass these tests.
Orks falling back can attempt to regroup as normal, but may also instead fall back towards any Ork mob that lies behind their position. If any Orks in the withdrawing unit get within 6" of the new mob once moves are complete then the withdrawing mob attempts to join with the new one. Roll 2D6 again the Leadership value of the falling back mob. If successful the two mobs combing together into one unit. The previously withdrawing mob can immediately move up to 6" to be in coherency with the second unit.
Only Ork foot units will mob up in this manner. Slavers and Meks in Grot mobs or Big Gunz, Stormboyz and Warbikes may not mob up.
A mob of Orks that mobs up with another unit counts as destroyed for victory points purposes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7bb4-34ca-51f3-bb8c" name="The Power of the WAAAGH!" hidden="false">
      <description>When an Ork mob charges into close combat roll a 2D6. If the score is equal to or under the number of Orks in the mob they charge in with a rousing "Waaaaaaaaagh!". All the Orks in the mob double their Initiative characteristic for the remainder of the assault phase. In future phases their Initiative returns to normal.
Orks who make sweeping advanced into the enemy also tests for The Power of the WAAAGH!. The test is made at the beginning of the assault phase so any casualties from enemy first will reduce the chances of them maintaining their momentum.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="496b-e8d5-33fe-9edb" name="Gretchin Mobs" hidden="false">
      <description>Gretchin who fail a Moral check caused by enemy shooting or tank shock or which fail to regroup after falling back from close combat the grots "go to ground." Remove all of the gretchin models from the board. If no slaver is present the mob is destroyed. If a slaver is present they remain on the board and attempts to regroup each turn, even if the Gretchin mob had been reduced below 50% starting strength or the enemy are within 6" 
The slaver trying to regroup the Gretchin mob cannot move, shoot or initiate an assault, but can be shot at or charged. They fight back in close combat as normal. If the slaver is killed the Gretchin unit is now destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="60e6-4b60-c541-3afb" name="Slippery" hidden="false">
      <description>Kommandos sneak through cover quickly and easily, so they roll an extra D6 when they move through difficult ground.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="249e-3d2c-b96b-7edc" name="Tank Hunters" hidden="false">
      <description>The mob always passed Tank Shock tests and adds +1 to all Armor Penetration rolls.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="cd1b-12a9-0ceb-301d" name="Living Shield" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Ork mobs which are shot at "through" a Grot mob can claim a 5+ cover save. Each successful save causes a Grot to be removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="39ee-155c-f8e8-f5c1" name="Better Footing" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Grot mob is in difficult ground any Ork mobs moving through the same difficult ground my re-roll the dice for how far they move. Mega Armored Orks may not use this ability.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c948-4917-842b-6b56" name="Mine Clearance" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Grot mob moves into a minefield remove 3D6 Grots as casualties and then remove the minefield marker. If there are fewer Grots remaining in the mob than the rolled dice than the Grot mob is destroyed and the minefield is not removed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d491-6e1b-3887-ae83" name="Bailin' Out" hidden="false">
      <description>Trukk Boyz suffer a wound on a D6 roll of 6 instead of a 4+ if their Trukk is destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1487-add8-d98b-7898" name="Short Ranged" hidden="false">
      <description>Warbike's Big Shootas are limited to a maximum rang eof 18".</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d2e0-6a69-f681-96f4" name="Hard to Hit" hidden="false">
      <description>Due to dust and exhaust clouds Warbikes give their riders a 5+ cover saving throw. Furthermore a unit being shot at "through" the warbikes also receive the 5+ cover saving throw.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8495-8dc4-d36b-5f4e" name="Speed Freeks" hidden="false">
      <description>Warbike Mobz are immune to the effects of morale and pinning.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2502-cef3-ea93-ab5d" name="Psycho Blastas" hidden="false">
      <description>In an assault Warbikers use their big shootas to blast the enemy at point blank range. Warbikers that charge into close combat strike first and make a shooting attack in the first round of combat instead of fighting normally.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8921-5e15-774b-8939" name="Hits on the Battery" hidden="false">
      <description>When a battary of Big Gunz is fired at, randomize any hits between the krew and the gunz. Roll a D6:
1-4: Hits the Krew
5-6: Hits a Big Gun
Hits against the Gunz is treated like a vehicle with an armor value of 10, but any glancing or penetrating hits destroy them.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="61d8-84e4-5a1f-6657" name="Looted Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>If a 1 is rolled to hit with a looted weapon the hit is scored on the shooting unit instead of the target.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e650-1e91-c401-41a1" name="Looted Vehicles" hidden="false">
      <description>Make a Breakdown test for each looted vehicle at the start of each turn. On a result of 1 on a D6 roll another D6. On a 1 the vehicle may not move this turn, and automatically fails their Breakdown test next turn. On the result of 2-3 the vehicle may not move this turn. On the result of 4-6 the vehicle lurches directly foward 2D6". Make Dangerous Terrain, Tank Shock, etc. as if the vehicle were moving normally. The vehicle may not making any further moves this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="aa19-c270-13f1-6356" name="Choppa" hidden="false">
      <description>In close combat an enemy model wounded by a Choppa has a maximum armor save of 4+. Any 2+ or 3+ armor saves are instead reduced to 4+. Armor saves of 5+, 6+ or - are not changed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="173b-0e54-5eea-964e" name="More Dakka" hidden="false">
      <description>More Dakka kustomisin' makes a shoota or slugga Assault 2 instead of rapid fire or pistol. A More Dakka kustom job combined with a Shootier kustom job  would produce a S5, Assault 2 shoota or slugga.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bc5b-2941-29a7-ce0b" name="Shootier" hidden="false">
      <description>Shootier weapons makes a shoota or slugga S5 instead of S4.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9907-7c8b-718f-0156" name="Blasta" hidden="false">
      <description>A shoota or slugga with the Blasta kustom job increases the armor piecing to AP3 at targets up to 12" and AP2 at targets up to 6". But a shoota or slugga with the Blasta kustom job gains the Get Hot! rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e312-e1c4-31fb-733d" name="'Eavy Armor" hidden="false">
      <description>An Ork wearing 'Eavy Armor has a 4+ Armor Save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4a24-7d6e-a253-5ace" name="Grot Bombs" hidden="false">
      <description>Treated as a Smart Bomb. You may re-roll the scatter dice if you don't like the first result, but you must accept the second result.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
